{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/903033-show-of-power-exploit-and-2e-mage-magic","id":903033,"title":"Show of power exploit and 2e mage magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T15:01:31-07:00","id":903033,"title":"Show of power exploit and 2e mage magic","content":"First off show of power allows you to mimic any power of other supernaturals as long as you have seen it. The drawback is that you can only ever get one sucess.<br /> <br /> Now since the intent of this seems to be that you display a power at the minimum ability how should show of power work with mage magic?<br /> <br /> Either you mimic the power exactly as you saw it, so your effect has the same variables or you are limited to the base spell. Mage magic only requires one sucess after all to suceed. Of course a demon if they could mimic a spell as they saw it that would be all they could do. They could not alter the variables and only display a spell exactly as they have seen it.<br /> <br /> The main reason I am curious on everyone else's interpretation is this could be a way for a demon to achieve hell. By mimicking a mage who cast the spell pocket dimension at max variables the demon could have a neighborhood sized area free of the machine, like a gaint bolt hole. Of course I feel this exact usage would be better with a gadget as the linchpin of this pocket dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:04:22-07:00","id":903145,"title":"","content":"I'd say that you replicate it, as it was performed, but otherwise minimum spell factors. Even if you saw it performed by a master Mage, too bad, you still only get the minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:17:05-07:00","id":903156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/903033-show-of-power-exploit-and-2e-mage-magic?p=903145#post903145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that you replicate it, as it was performed, but otherwise minimum spell factors. Even if you saw it performed by a master Mage, too bad, you still only get the minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you replicate it as preformed then you replicate it with the spell factors you witnessed not the minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:34:04-07:00","id":903212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/903033-show-of-power-exploit-and-2e-mage-magic?p=903156#post903156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you replicate it as preformed then you replicate it with the spell factors you witnessed not the minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify.<br /> <br /> You replicate the <i>effect</i> of the spell. But you replicate its effects at the lowest possible spell factors. So you could replicate, say, a <i>Kinetic Blow</i> cast with the Reach for the Stunned Tilt and Advanced duration, but you would be limited to +1 damage, one scene duration and one subject, even if it was cast with much higher spell factors originally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}